From bbef564768b6d9b402592a7c6a6781ffa47f5950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:59:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(bridge): recursive prop encoding for nested node
 refs and callbacks

Functions, orphan JSX nodes and handles are now encoded as tagged refs at
any depth of a prop value ({$fn: path}, {$node: id}, {$handle: id}) and
decoded once in applyOps, so FuseMap accessors (callback, widget,
widgetList, handle, mapList) work on nested objects and lists.

- handlers live on their node, keyed by path, and are released on remove,
  slot drop, handle dispose and unmount (the global map used to leak)
- slot nodes are owned per prop; handles are borrowed and no longer
  disposed when a widget referencing them goes away
- the boolean `true` callback marker is gone from the wire; Dart still
  accepts it and {_node} from older bundles

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UAn6VGsSjV5tprf9ZbdxaB
