From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:15:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(bridge): experimental synchronous Dart-to-JS calls
 and list builders

fjs: JsEngine.call_global_sync (frb sync) runs a global JS function on the
caller's thread under the runtime lock, with a lowered JS stack budget;
queued jobs and bridge calls are left to the background driver.

solid-fuse: FuseCallback.callSync / FuseMap.syncCallback route through
__fuseCallSync, which returns [value, ops] so nodes a builder creates are
applied inside the same Flutter build. Two experimental ListView.builder
projections (sync builder, windowed virtualization) plus an integration
test that measures both against the real engine.

